# /etc/datahub/flow.env
#
# JVM flags for datahub@flow (intellistream-flow): a fixed heap, pre-touched on the NUMA node the
# placement drop-in binds it to.
#
# Unlike the other services, most of this one's working memory is off-heap: a run's data lives in
# Arrow memory, which is direct memory, and the JVM caps all direct memory together with
# MaxDirectMemorySize (by default the heap size). The service refuses to start unless its Arrow
# budget (datahub.flow.arrow.budget in /etc/datahub/flow/application.yml) plus the Pulsar client's
# 512 MB plus headroom fits under that cap, so set it here explicitly and keep the two in step.
#
# The last two flags are what Arrow needs on Java 25: its IPC path wraps Arrow memory in NIO
# buffers through a private java.nio constructor, and it allocates through sun.misc.Unsafe.
# No heap dump on OOM (the JVM default); see "Diagnostics" in the README.
JAVA_OPTS=-Xms8g -Xmx8g -XX:MaxDirectMemorySize=8g -XX:+AlwaysPreTouch -XX:+UseTransparentHugePages -XX:+UseCompactObjectHeaders -XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError --add-opens=java.base/java.nio=ALL-UNNAMED --sun-misc-unsafe-memory-access=allow
